1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,000
Zoha — It’s 06:00. Five hundred guests arrive today.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:08,200
Zoha — The delivery cut-off is closing. One wrong guess could stop service.

3
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:13,800
Omar — So the chef takes one photo. Front Door reads it and checks Valio.

4
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:18,600
Omar — Then it puts the decision back in the chef’s hands.

5
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:24,000
Zoha — Gemini reads the handwriting, finds the seven items, and keeps the exception visible.

6
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:32,000
Omar — The agent checks price, stock, delivery date, and pack sizes.

7
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:39,000
Omar — The score is a check on what the chef meant.

8
00:00:40,000 --> 00:00:47,000
Zoha — The milk line is above the kitchen’s 1,500 euro limit. The door holds the cart.

9
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Omar — A short or uncertain line is not silently replaced. The card explains the safe next choice.

10
00:00:56,000 --> 00:01:01,000
Zoha — The agent cannot approve. The chef can.

11
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:09,000
Omar — The order is confirmed, signed, and recorded for the kitchen and Valio.

12
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:39,000
Zoha — The Decisions score sets when the agent may act alone. Code still controls money, stock, dates, and approval.

13
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:44,500
Omar — Codex built the core we just used: the engine, the Gemini agent, and the safety paths.

14
00:01:44,700 --> 00:01:49,000
Zoha — CRACI runs the build checks and ties the order to its build evidence.

15
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:53,000
Omar — The order is confirmed.

16
00:01:53,000 --> 00:01:57,000
Zoha — At 06:00, the chef is still in control.

